#26143
Peak of Thangorodrim~
   Your breath is taken away as you stand upon some high hard horn of 
the world.  The lands below are covered in mists, lofty snowcapped peaks 
surround you.  As you blink sleepily in the sun, you can hear a voice 
coming from above.
   Looking up and behind you, your heart is pierced with pity.  There, 
above a sheer cliff, rests a mighty black chair.  Sitting within is a 
man, an old beaten man, whose eyes stare blankly ahead to something not 
in this place or this time.  He appears once to have been a haughty 
warrior, now withered with many years of imprisonment and torture upon 
the peak.  However, he has not been broken, for he is still hale and his 
face is proud.
   This undoubtedly is Hurin, he who dared to ride alone to the very 
Gates of Thangorodrim, only to be captured and set upon the rock.  For 
fifty long years he has been here, seeing only what Melkor would allow 
him, forced to live only for his and his family's torment.
~
260 4 -1 0 0 0 0 5
