0 -1 26142
E
hurin~
     Hurin, still looking forward, struggles to speak through
parched lips.
"....that you have come here and achieved a great deed of
which the minstrels shall sing.  None could have foreseen what
has come to pass through your valour and might.  For these
things which you have wrested from Him are of worth greater
than you can comprehend, and are treasured by Him above
all else.  Yea, these are the very jewels which Feanor himself
wrought in Valinor in times long passed."
     Hurin pauses, as if stirred by some bittersweet memory.
"These, brave travelers, are the Silmarils, they in which
the full splendor of the Two Trees is captured forever; that
glory cannot be regained, for Melkor poisoned the Trees
and put out their light.  These are they which caused many bitter
wars, where kinsmen fought each other for their possession.
Although they have great power unto themselves individually,
when combined, their might is redoubled in force.  The
legends speak of a mighty smith who lives within the mightiest
forest in this region of the world.  He can set the three in a casing
which will ensure that the Silmarils will never fade.  His name
is Telchontar...."
     You see a tear run down Hurin's proud face.
"Go now, my friends.  My doom is well nigh, and it is not within
your power, nor any power within the world as it now exists, to
change it.  Leave me to drink the bitter cup which has been
set before me."
     Hurin says no more.
~
